                <pb facs="0632" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/8–2144:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Sweden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-22T13:00:00-04:00">August 22, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1676. Your 3217, August 21. Provided British concur we agree to Madame
                    Kollontay’s suggested amendment to joint message.</p>
                <p>Sent to Stockholm, repeated to London as No. 6671 of August 22, 1 p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
